## ⚡ Installation & Setup

### 1️⃣ Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/gaitsecure.git
cd gaitsecure
2️⃣ Mobile App Setup
npm install -g expo-cli
npm install
expo start
3️⃣ Backend Setup
python -m venv gaitsecure_env
source gaitsecure_env/bin/activate   # Windows: gaitsecure_env\Scripts\activate

pip install -r requirements.txt
python train_model.py
python app.py
🔌 API Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/	Server status
GET	/health	Health check
POST	/predict	Authenticate gait
GET	/users	List users
POST	/models/reload	Reload models
🧠 Machine Learning Pipeline
Feature Extraction
Mean, Standard Deviation
Min, Max, Median
Step count detection
Walking frequency
Spectral energy
Models Used
Support Vector Machine (SVM)
Random Forest Classifier
📊 Data Format
[
  {
    "x": -0.123,
    "y": 9.456,
    "z": 0.789,
    "type": "accel",
    "timestamp": 1634567890123
  }
]
📂 Project Structure
gaitsecure/
├── mobile/
│   ├── App.js
│   ├── screens/
│   └── utils/
├── backend/
│   ├── app.py
│   ├── train_model.py
│   ├── utils.py
│   └── data/
└── README.md
🚀 Usage Workflow
1. Record Gait
Open app → Start recording
Walk for ~5 seconds
Data saved locally
2. Train Model
Move data to backend/data/
Run:
python train_model.py
3. Authenticate
Select recorded walk
Send to backend
Receive prediction + confidence
📈 Performance
Accuracy: 85–95%
Prediction Time: <500ms
Feature Count: ~48
🛡️ Security Considerations
Data stored locally
No personal information transmitted
Input validation implemented
API endpoints protected
🔧 Configuration

Update backend URL in mobile app:

fetch('http://<YOUR_IP>:5000/predict')
🔍 Troubleshooting
Server not connecting → Check IP and network
Low accuracy → Collect more training data
Model errors → Ensure .pkl files exist
🚧 Future Enhancements
Cloud sync
Anti-spoof detection
Wearable device integration
Multi-factor authentication
